<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:45:46 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>In Brazil, thousands march fearing return of Bolsonaro presidency</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/in-brazil-thousands-march-fearing-return-of-bolsonaro-presidency</link><description>
Thousands of young Brazilians have taken to the streets to support President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and voice fears of a return to power for the Bolsonaro political movement, amid a closely watched presidential race. Many protesters say they are worried about their future, particularly the impact a far-right government could have on universities and education. FRANCE 24’s Jan Onoszko reports from Brazil.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a900a94-c715-11f1-ae5c-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-162050-162633-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a900a94-c715-11f1-ae5c-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-162050-162633-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6ff87552-c715-11f1-b7f0-ff2b36bbad19</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:59:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump’s use of Russian diesel fuel, at Ukraine’s expense, sparks controversy in the US</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-s-use-of-russian-diesel-fuel-at-ukraine-s-expense-sparks-controversy-in-the-us</link><description>
Donald Trump’s plan to import Russian diesel despite Western sanctions has sparked fierce criticism in Washington, including from Republicans, as high fuel prices and the upcoming midterm elections put pressure on his administration. His approach to the Ukraine war has also drawn controversy, with calls for Kyiv to hold elections and claims of an energy ceasefire announced without clear agreement from the parties involved. FRANCE 24's Douglas Herbert has the analysis.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1050b6b8-c707-11f1-8d3f-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-131555-132004-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1050b6b8-c707-11f1-8d3f-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-131555-132004-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1588b1d0-c707-11f1-98cd-b1c2e58f18c5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:26:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US economists win Nobel for research helping policymakers navigate crises</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-economists-win-nobel-for-research-helping-policymakers-navigate-crises</link><description>
Two American economists, Robert E. Hall of Stanford University and Michael Woodford of Columbia University, have won the Nobel Memorial Prize in Economic Sciences for their work on economic stabilisation. Their research helps policymakers and central banks better understand economic fluctuations, manage recessions and inflation, and account for public expectations when shaping economic policy. The prize money, worth around $1.2 million, will be shared equally between the two laureates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/81e7cf3c-c6e9-11f1-9fbf-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-111231-111403-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/81e7cf3c-c6e9-11f1-9fbf-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-111231-111403-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">86fcb47e-c6e9-11f1-933e-7d8170ba1900</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:04:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US immigration authorities raid home of Democratic Trump critic Ilhan Omar</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-immigration-authorities-raid-home-of-democratic-trump-critic-ilhan-omar</link><description>
US authorities raided the Washington home of Democratic Representative Ilhan Omar on Monday as part of an ongoing investigation into alleged immigration fraud, according to reports. The probe reportedly includes immigration paperwork completed by her late father when she was a child. Omar accused the Trump administration of using government institutions to target political opponents, describing the raid as an act of political intimidation. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson has the latest from Washington.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/079d169a-c64b-11f1-b93c-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26285444534618.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/079d169a-c64b-11f1-b93c-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26285444534618.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7c134b0c-c6eb-11f1-9c35-a78921356c9c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:57:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>'Breaking Bad' actor and disability activist RJ Mitte dies aged 34</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-breaking-bad-actor-and-disability-activist-rj-mitte-dies-aged-34</link><description>
"Breaking Bad" actor RJ Mitte, who played Walter White Jr. in the hit US television series, has died aged 34, his representatives said Monday. The actor, who lived with cerebal palsy, also became a prominent disability rights advocate, championing inclusion and representation in film and television.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ae51ebe-c69e-11f1-8ce7-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25157102255151.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ae51ebe-c69e-11f1-8ce7-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25157102255151.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6f2ece1e-c6a7-11f1-8abe-a993eb2b6dc5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 01:43:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ae51ebe-c69e-11f1-8ce7-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25157102255151.jpg">© Andy Kropa, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US federal agents raid home of Democratic congresswoman and Trump critic Ilhan Omar</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261012-us-federal-agents-raid-home-of-democratic-congresswoman-and-trump-critic-ilhan-omar</link><description>
US federal agents on Monday launched a raid on ‌the Washington home of Democratic representative Ilhan Omar, an outspoken critic of US President Donald ⁠Trump, officials said. The raid followed a criminal fraud ‌investigation into the Somali-born lawmaker's immigration paperwork submitted by her late father when she ⁠was a child, Fox News reported.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/079d169a-c64b-11f1-b93c-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26285444534618.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/079d169a-c64b-11f1-b93c-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26285444534618.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1def716e-c64a-11f1-9789-2b1c4558ec34</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:13:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/079d169a-c64b-11f1-b93c-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26285444534618.jpg">© J. Scott Applewhite, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Capital punishment in US: Elected judges, prosecutors seek 'results', 'not interested in the truth'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261012-capital-punishment-in-us-elected-judges-prosecutors-seek-results-not-interested-in-the-truth</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Sandrine Ageorges-Skinner, an advocate against the death penalty, author and member of the association "Ensemble contre la peine de mort" (Together Against the Death Penalty). She asserts that capital punishment is "really a political agenda, especially in electoral times."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fdbc9c0a-c707-11f1-aa6c-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e3a068e9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fdbc9c0a-c707-11f1-aa6c-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e3a068e9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bdd8c1e4-c640-11f1-b150-373a4bc443aa</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:27:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Inside Jeffrey Epstein's network: How favours, money and influence kept it running</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261012-inside-jeffrey-epstein-s-network-how-favours-money-and-influence-kept-it-running</link><description>
For years, convicted sexual predator Jeffrey Epstein developed a global web of powerful connections despite accusations of sex trafficking. Millions of declassified documents reveal how he expanded and maintainted his network.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2871ea94-c619-11f1-b505-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/01-62.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2871ea94-c619-11f1-b505-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/01-62.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b62f09e8-c619-11f1-8e54-6765c25dfd25</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:36:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2871ea94-c619-11f1-b505-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/01-62.png">© France 24</source><dc:creator>Ava LUQUET</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Brazil's Lula accuses social media giant Meta of election interference amid tight run-off campaign</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261011-brazil-lula-accuses-social-media-giant-meta-election-interference-amid-tight-run-campaign</link><description>
Social media platform Meta has 48 hours to respond to claims by Brazil's leftwing candidate and incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's campaign accusing the tech platform of blocking content on the company's platforms. Brazil's Superior Electoral Court on Saturday gave the social media giant 48 hours to clarify whether it reduced the reach of posts by Lula's campaign ahead of the tight October 25 run-off against rightwing candidate Flavio Bolsonaro. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c380a90-c56f-11f1-a8f8-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36TD3C3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c380a90-c56f-11f1-a8f8-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36TD3C3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eda9e804-c56d-11f1-8ad3-0dfce67db219</guid><pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:12:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c380a90-c56f-11f1-a8f8-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36TD3C3.jpg">© Kirill Kudryavtsev, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Convicted murderer Christa Pike leaves hospital, returns to prison after botched execution</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261010-convicted-murderer-christa-pike-leaves-hospital-returns-to-prison-after-botched-execution</link><description>
Christa Pike's lawyers on Saturday said that the 50-year-old convicted murderer has been discharged from the hospital and returned to prison. Pike was transported to the hospital in critical condition on September 30 after she survived Tennessee's botched effort to execute her for murdering a classmate when she was a teenager. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fc50584-c4cd-11f1-bae9-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-06T220818Z-71220444-RC2PTNAKF4UE-RTRMADP-3-TENNESSEE-EXECUTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fc50584-c4cd-11f1-bae9-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-06T220818Z-71220444-RC2PTNAKF4UE-RTRMADP-3-TENNESSEE-EXECUTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f7a15c92-c4ce-11f1-b11c-391c64cb86c6</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:41:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fc50584-c4cd-11f1-bae9-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-06T220818Z-71220444-RC2PTNAKF4UE-RTRMADP-3-TENNESSEE-EXECUTION.jpg">© J. Miles Cary, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US, Europe and Ukraine hold 'constructive discussions' on joint plan to end war</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261010-us-ukrainians-europeans-discuss-new-ideas-to-end-war-diesel</link><description>
US, Ukrainian and European negotiators held talks in Miami on Friday to seek a common proposal to end the war in Ukraine, as President Donald Trump's decision to ease restrictions on Russian fuel drew criticism from lawmakers and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/69175476-c47f-11f1-a476-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T050009Z-1359303607-RC2SDNA1852R-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-EUROPE-GAS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/69175476-c47f-11f1-a476-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T050009Z-1359303607-RC2SDNA1852R-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-EUROPE-GAS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0e9ab8ea-c47e-11f1-b3d1-650afb66e3ea</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 07:47:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/69175476-c47f-11f1-a476-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T050009Z-1359303607-RC2SDNA1852R-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-EUROPE-GAS.jpg">© Valentyn Ogirenko, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Powerful 7.6 magnitude quake shakes Panama, triggering tsunami warnings</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-powerful-7-6-magnitude-quake-shakes-panama-triggering-tsunami-warning</link><description>
A strong 7.6 magnitude earthquake struck near the southern ​coast ‌of Panama ⁠on Friday at a 10 km depth, ‌according to the US Geological ⁠Survey, shaking buildings as far away as the capital and prompting evacuations. The US Tsunami Warning ​System showed potential tsunami threats across much of Central America's Pacific ​coast.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e685866-c417-11f1-a54f-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-09T190605Z-119910366-RC2UZNAG2SLO-RTRMADP-3-PANAMA-QUAKE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e685866-c417-11f1-a54f-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-09T190605Z-119910366-RC2UZNAG2SLO-RTRMADP-3-PANAMA-QUAKE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">26ce30f4-c410-11f1-bc25-adb65edd2195</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 18:39:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e685866-c417-11f1-a54f-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-09T190605Z-119910366-RC2UZNAG2SLO-RTRMADP-3-PANAMA-QUAKE.jpg">© Enea Lebrun, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Unweaving Jeffrey Epstein’s web: What the files have revealed</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-unweaving-jeffrey-epstein-s-web-what-the-files-have-revealed</link><description>
On January 30, 2026, the US Justice Department released 3 million documents. Photos, videos, emails, text messages, court records... All connected to one man: Jeffrey Epstein. Since then, media outlets around the world have brought to light the vast amount of people that appear in the Epstein files. Eight months on, what what do these revelations tell us about Jeffrey Epstein’s network? How did it operate? FRANCE 24 journalist Ava Luquet spent months digging through the files. In this video, she takes a closer look at what they reveal about the predator’s network and its inner workings.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/146a2ab2-c27b-11f1-b11f-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/EPSTEIN-EN-vignette-2.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/146a2ab2-c27b-11f1-b11f-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/EPSTEIN-EN-vignette-2.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c8fad210-c26c-11f1-b49f-dd754fbf8bc3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 17:00:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pentagon vows to livestream first military execution in decades</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-pentagon-vows-to-livestream-first-military-execution-in-decades</link><description>
The first US military execution in more than 65 years will be livestreamed, announced the Pentagon on Thursday, after Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth said it would be "public".
 
Former Army psychiatrist Nidal Hasan opened fire at Fort Hood in Texas in 2009, killing 13 people. His execution will take place at the military base on December 3, 2026.
 
 "The livestreaming of an execution is tantamount to a public execution and would breach the absolute prohibition of torture," the Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights said on Friday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7d18288-c3ca-11f1-98a3-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/Nidal-Hasan-execution00.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7d18288-c3ca-11f1-98a3-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/Nidal-Hasan-execution00.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fcb4c3ae-c3ca-11f1-a485-5fede210fc06</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 10:56:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Hegseth says Fort Hood shooter's military execution will be 'livestreamed'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261009-hegseth-says-fort-hood-shooter-s-military-execution-will-be-livestreamed</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Friday, October 9: US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth announces that the military execution of Fort Hood shooter Nidal Malik Hasan will be "livestreamed". But first: we look at reactions in Italy after the country's parliament passes a controversial electoral reform that critics say serves to benefit Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni. Plus, ".fart" and ".trump" are among the new domain name applications, as revealed by the US non-profit organisation ICANN.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e16ad984-c3a8-11f1-b25e-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-10-09T05-24-48-707Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e16ad984-c3a8-11f1-b25e-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-10-09T05-24-48-707Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">baebf904-c3a4-11f1-9854-e54348da6a12</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 09:39:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>New York mayor to ask Trump for ICE withdrawal after agents shoot man in car with child</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-new-york-mayor-calls-for-ice-removal-after-man-shot-with-5-year-old-nearby</link><description>
New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani has said he will ask US President Donald Trump to remove ICE from the city after federal immigration agents on Thursday shot a man in a vehicle with his five-year-old child during an attempted arrest. The 28-year-old survived and is being treated at hospital.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37d03862-c3a1-11f1-8aea-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/8486a05cfb4b866ec0c054f68d6f50c81cd6e869.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37d03862-c3a1-11f1-8aea-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/8486a05cfb4b866ec0c054f68d6f50c81cd6e869.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">387903d4-c3a1-11f1-9773-fdd622757476</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 05:21:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37d03862-c3a1-11f1-8aea-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/8486a05cfb4b866ec0c054f68d6f50c81cd6e869.jpg">© Charly Triballeau, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Brazil's Flavio Bolsonaro wins support of third-place candidate in presidential race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-brazil-flavio-bolsonaro-third-place-candidate-lula</link><description>
Brazil's right-wing presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro secured third-place finisher Augusto Cury's endorsement on Thursday, strengthening his position against incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva ahead of the runoff. Cury won nearly three percent in Sunday's first round. A Datafolha poll put Bolsonaro ahead with 52 percent against Lula's 48 percent.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0239c2c6-c0d2-11f1-a18d-578a4b968fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/9c62a0873c3a5fa709668a9df3a59e89ea25bf23.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0239c2c6-c0d2-11f1-a18d-578a4b968fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/9c62a0873c3a5fa709668a9df3a59e89ea25bf23.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0862e5ec-c389-11f1-a6a7-e7e75acda77d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 02:34:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0239c2c6-c0d2-11f1-a18d-578a4b968fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/9c62a0873c3a5fa709668a9df3a59e89ea25bf23.jpg">© Evaristo Sa, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Families reunited as USS Lincoln returns from troubled 10-month deployment</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-families-reunited-as-uss-lincoln-comes-home-after-troubled-gulf-deployment</link><description>
The USS Lincoln docked in California on Thursday ending a record deployment of 265 days of uninterrupted time at sea marked by reports of deteriorating conditions onboard. Crew members were reunited with family they had not seen in nearly a year after their mission was prolonged by the war in Iran.
